{"step_index":45,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T05:31:49Z","thinking":"Focus is now on creating the `app.js` file and ensuring all required functionalities are implemented. This starts with defining realistic initial data for subjects, including conducted and attended sessions, attendance percentages, and associated safety statuses. This data will be crucial for simulating a student's academic performance.\n\n\nInitial subject data suggests attendance risks in COA, requiring immediate attention. The assignment list reveals a critical, immediate Java report deadline alongside pending DBMS, Data Structures, DSD, and COA tasks, requiring priority assessment. The timetable information will be integrated to predict the best time to schedule work and identify potential conflicts.\n\n\nAnalyzing the timetable and exam schedules, I'll integrate this data into the performance simulation. This includes identifying time conflicts and optimizing study time allocation. The canteen data might influence lunch break scheduling, which will be integrated in the analysis to keep up with the data.\n\n\nChecking assignment status and upcoming deadlines is the first step. User login state will determine the initial screen; remembered logins go to the main app, others to the login screen. Data persistence for login credentials is required.\n\nThe login page will pre-fill student information if available. Upon successful login, the application will display a welcome message and a toast notification indicating the login status. A guest login option provides instant access.\nThe dashboard will dynamically calculate a survival score based on attendance, pending assignments, exam proximity, and completed tasks. Today's timetable will be automatically loaded. Also included will be a countdown to the next exam and a \"SHOULD I SLEEP OR STUDY?\" button.\n\n\nAttendance calculations will be integrated using formulas for percentage calculation, missed class determination (given 75% threshold), and required consecutive attendance. Assignment countdowns will utilize deadline sorting with status badges and completion toggles. Canteen data includes operational status, quotes, menu items, and a calculator.\n\nTimetable functionality will implement day-based tab navigation and automated highlighting for the current day. Live exam countdowns will display time remaining. The survival engine will include study break suggestions.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"/**\n * 🎓 Student Survival App 🧑🎓🔥\n * Tagline: “Survive college. One deadline at a time. 😂”\n * \n * Complete modular client-side application engine\n * - State management with localStorage persistence\n * - Realistic college sample data\n * - Rigorous mathematical attendance calculations\n * - Real-time countdown tickers (ticking every second)\n * - Sleep or Study Survival AI decision engine\n * - Web Audio API sound synthesis\n * - Mobile bottom nav & responsive tab routing\n */\n\nconst App = (function() {\n  'use strict';\n\n  // ==========================================\n  // 1. DEFAULT REALISTIC SAMPLE DATA\n  // ==========================================\n  const DEFAULT_STUDENT = {\n    name: 'Aarav Sharma',\n    email: 'aarav.sharma@college.edu',\n    college: 'Institute of Engineering & Technology',\n    branch: 'Computer Science & Engineering',\n    semester: 'Semester 4',\n    isLoggedIn: false,\n    rememberMe: true,\n    soundEnabled: true,\n  };\n\n  const DEFAULT_SUBJECTS = [\n    { id: 'sub-1', name: 'DBMS (CS301)', total: 40, attended: 32 },       // 80.0% - Safe (can miss 2)\n    { id: 'sub-2', name: 'Data Structures (DS)', total: 36, attended: 27 },// 75.0% - Safe (0 margin)\n    { id: 'sub-3', name: 'Digital System Design (DSD)', total: 32, attended: 22 }, // 68.75% - Warning (need 8)\n    { id: 'sub-4', name: 'Value Added Course (VAC)', total: 20, attended: 18 },    // 90.0% - Safe (can miss 4)\n    { id: 'sub-5', name: 'OOP / Java', total: 42, attended: 36 },           // 85.7% - Safe (can miss 6)\n    { id: 'sub-6', name: 'COA (CS304)', total: 35, attended: 21 },         // 60.0% - Danger (need 21)\n  ];\n\n  // Helper to generate dates relative to today\n  function getFutureDate(daysAhead, hours = 23, mins = 59) {\n    const d = new Date();\n    d.setDate(d.getDate() + daysAhead);\n    d.setHours(hours, mins, 0, 0);\n    return d.toISOString();\n  }\n\n  const DEFAULT_ASSIGNMENTS = [\n    {\n      id: 'asg-1',\n      title: 'DBMS Normalization & ER Diagram Project',\n      subject: 'DBMS',\n      dueDate: getFutureDate(2, 23, 59), // 2 days left\n      priority: 'High',\n      completed: false,\n    },\n    {\n      id: 'asg-2',\n      title: 'Red-Black Trees & Heap Sort Implementation',\n      subject: 'Data Structures (DS)',\n      dueDate: getFutureDate(0, 23, 59), // Due today!\n      priority: 'High',\n      completed: false,\n    },\n    {\n      id: 'asg-3',\n      title: 'Sequential Circuit State Machine Design',\n      subject: 'Digital System Design (DSD)',\n      dueDate: getFutureDate(5, 17, 0), // 5 days left\n      priority: 'Medium',\n      completed: false,\n    },\n    {\n      id: 'asg-4',\n      title: 'Java Multithreading & Socket Programming Lab',\n      subject: 'OOP / Java',\n      dueDate: getFutureDate(7, 23, 59), // 7 days left\n      priority: 'Medium',\n      completed: false,\n    },\n    {\n      id: 'asg-5',\n      title: 'MIPS Instruction Pipeline & Cache Simulation',\n      subject: 'Computer Organization & Architecture (COA)',\n      dueDate: getFutureDate(11, 23, 59),\n      priority: 'Low',\n      completed: false,\n    },\n    {\n      id: 'asg-6',\n      title: 'Ethics & Sustainable Tech Case Study',\n      subject: 'Value Added Course (VAC)',\n      dueDate: getFutureDate(-2, 23, 59),\n      priority: 'Low',\n      completed: true,\n    }\n  ];\n\n  const DEFAULT_CANTEEN = {\n    isOpen: true,\n    openingHours: '08:00 AM – 06:00 PM',\n    menu: [\n      { id: 'm-1', name: 'Maggi', emoji: '🍜', price: 40, category: 'Comfort Food' },\n      { id: 'm-2', name: 'Grilled Sandwich', emoji: '🥪', price: 50, category: 'Quick Bites' },\n      { id: 'm-3', name: 'Cheese Pizza', emoji: '🍕', price: 80, category: 'Cheat Meal' },\n      { id: 'm-4', name: 'Cold Coffee', emoji: '☕', price: 50, category: 'Caffeine Rush' },\n      { id: 'm-5', name: 'Cold Drink', emoji: '🥤', price: 30, category: 'Beverages' },\n      { id: 'm-6', name: 'Crispy French Fries', emoji: '🍟', price: 60, category: 'Snacks' },\n      { id: 'm-7', name: 'Samosa (2 pcs)', emoji: '🥟', price: 25, category: 'Campus Classic' },\n      { id: 'm-8', name: 'Cutting Chai', emoji: '🧃', price: 15, category: 'Life Support' },\n      { id: 'm-9', name: 'Veg Patties', emoji: '🥐', price: 25, category: 'Quick Bites' },\n    ]\n  };\n\n  const DEFAULT_TIMETABLE = [\n    // Monday\n    { id: 'tt-1', day: 'Monday', time: '09:00 - 10:00', subject: 'DBMS', room: 'Room 302', faculty: 'Dr. Sharma' },\n    { id: 'tt-2', day: 'Monday', time: '10:00 - 11:00', subject: 'Data Structures (DS)', room: 'Room 305', faculty: 'Prof. Anjali' },\n    { id: 'tt-3', day: 'Monday', time: '11:00 - 12:00', subject: 'Break / Canteen Rush ☕', room: 'Campus Lawn', faculty: 'Self Care' },\n    { id: 'tt-4', day: 'Monday', time: '12:00 - 01:00', subject: 'OOP / Java', room: 'Room 401', faculty: 'Dr. Kulkarni' },\n    { id: 'tt-5', day: 'Monday', time: '02:00 - 04:00', subject: 'COA Lab', room: 'Hardware Lab B', faculty: 'Prof. Mehta' },\n\n    // Tuesday\n    { id: 'tt-6', day: 'Tuesday', time: '09:00 - 10:00', subject: 'Digital System Design (DSD)', room: 'Room 204', faculty: 'Prof. Rao' },\n    { id: 'tt-7', day: 'Tuesday', time: '10:00 - 11:00', subject: 'OOP / Java', room: 'Room 401', faculty: 'Dr. Kulk